<title>CANADA: CMHC sets C$130 mln 5.0 percent bond due 2002.</title>
<headline>CMHC sets C$130 mln 5.0 percent bond due 2002.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Mortgage and Housing Corp on Thursday set a C$130 million, 5.0 percent medium-term note due January 2, 2002, on financial markets, lead manager RBC Dominion Securities said.</p>
<p>The issue was priced at C$97.442 plus one day accrued interest to yield 5.662 percent on a semi-annual basis. The issues was priced 3.6 basis points over the Government of Canada 7.0 percent bond due 2001.  </p>
<p>Payment and delivery of the new issue will be on February 3, 1997.</p>
<p>((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com))</p>
